        "node_id": "n_1_fd0b6f",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was due to an incorrect handling of the 'tight' condition. Let's refine our approach by considering all possible combinations of digits that could form the power of 2, and then count how many numbers up to n contain these combinations as substrings. This approach should correctly handle all cases, including the edge cases that caused the previous implementation to fail.",
